resources.string:
Muslim Shield uses the Android AccessibilityService API. This app is not an accessibility tool for people with disabilities; the API is used only to:

• capture the screen image to find faces in photos and videos;
• draw a blur over images of non-mahram people;
• read where photos are on the screen, so the blur moves with them while scrolling.

This data is processed only in the moment and only on the phone. It is not stored, not sent to the internet and not shared with anyone. The app does not collect messages, passwords or personal data, and it does not perform actions for you in other apps.

Optional “fast mode” does the same faster with screen-recording permission; those images are also not stored or sent.
